    "long_term_narrative": "Revenue growth has decelerated sharply, from a 5-year CAGR of 7.75% to a 3-year CAGR of 3.69% and just 1.87% year-over-year, even as margins have trended favorably (margin trend score of 100) and EPS grew 23.48% year-over-year. Profitability metrics like ROE (42.99%) and ROIC (16.35%) remain high, but the stock's valuation multiples (P/E 26.5, EV/EBITDA 20.7, P/B 10.5) sit well above what Graham-style and DCF fair-value models imply, producing large negative margins of safety (-71.99% Graham upside, -13.0% DCF upside). Leverage (debt-to-equity 1.20) adds some balance-sheet risk to weigh against the durable-seeming profitability. These offsetting factors are consistent with the model's Neutral long-term verdict (score 44.7).",
    "one_line_summary": "KO shows strong margins and ROE but trades at a premium to modeled fair value, with slowing top-line growth and mixed leverage.",
    "short_term_narrative": "Coca-Cola's price sits modestly above its 50-day average (+1.38%) and more clearly above its 200-day average (+11.47%), reflecting a period of price strength. The 3-month return of +11.16% contrasts with a slight -2.32% pullback over the past month, and the stock's momentum has outpaced its sector peers by about 6.91 percentage points. Trading volume has run about 1.79x its average, a supply/demand divergence worth noting without a known cause. Together these mixed signals support the model's Neutral short-term verdict (score 54)."
